// @expect-error Function 'main' returns 'long', but 'main' can only return 'int' or nothing, because what it returns becomes the program's exit code, the number the program ends with. Write 'main() -> int' to choose the exit code, or 'main()' to end with 0.
// The entry point's result is the process exit code, so only 'int' or no return type is legal.
main() -> long {
    return 42L;
}
